{"title":"2024 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 16","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(guessing_strategy)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (guessing strategy)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(OEEE)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (OEEE)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(EEEE)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (EEEE)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(Monovariants)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (Monovariants)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Solution_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Solution_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_Pi_Academy_(Fast_and_Easy_⚡🚀)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by Pi Academy (Fast and Easy ⚡🚀)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2 by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_3_by_Ani_lytical\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 3 by Ani_lytical</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Jerry likes to play with numbers. One day, he wrote all the integers from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/7/e5711c8d31d3bc3119aba377c9bda0f9dfb14e4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2024$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" /> on the whiteboard. Then he repeatedly chose four numbers on the whiteboard, erased them, and replaced them by either their sum or their product. (For example, Jerry's first step might have been to erase <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and then write either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, their sum, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, their product, on the whiteboard.) After repeatedly performing this operation, Jerry noticed that all the remaining numbers on the whiteboard were odd. What is the maximum possible number of integers on the whiteboard at that time?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/7/627442eb4ffc03e02969c8b7bff43eaa3f265b05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 1010 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } 1011 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } 1012 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } 1013 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } 1014$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"492\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider the numbers from 1 through 2024 in mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/8/d98447bb578a1a865a2cb427c09bfc8db6a39cf0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,0,1,0,...,1,0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"120\" height=\"17\" />. Note that the number of odd integers is monotonously decreasing.\n</p><p>We need to get rid of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/3/d83eeb9ab5890602a512b7735f593abec1dc6978.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1012$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />'s, so we either add or multiply four <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />s together to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/6/aa61ed1930d5727cc6c761b5b4d611064e7f13a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1012\\rightarrow 253 \\rightarrow 63+1=64 \\rightarrow 16 \\rightarrow 4 \\rightarrow 1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"340\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>To get rid of the final <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we need to consume three other <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />'s to result in one <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Thus the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/0/ab08ac082036abadd4a046a1bc4cd9eb4991a5b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1012-2=\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) } 1010 }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"177\" height=\"30\" />,\n</p><p>~Mintylemon66\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>(I will denote even numbers as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/a/a3a59bb1293ee3f6dec19de4019a7178874219ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> and odd numbers as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/a/39a710e66595fc1698f6d09b7f91ea01db604fcd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\normalsize o$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> for the purpose of this question, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> as the answer we need)\n</p><p>First, we observe that each time Jerry replaces four number with one (let's call this an \"<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/c/04c62d78405c31d894a49670a6d648150038432f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$operation$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"17\" />\"), we lose exactly three numbers regardless of the type of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/c/04c62d78405c31d894a49670a6d648150038432f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$operation$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"17\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/4/a2446c36c8a0223681d5c784da6ef9a1d2b8151c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Additive$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"71\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/a/19a1c4ce225eb48e68e8bf4610394e24a32011e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Multiplicative$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"120\" height=\"18\" />).\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/2/a72067a8d8debe8c45b4f3aac114e741b76481d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Rightarrow x \\equiv 2024 \\equiv 2\\pmod3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"202\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Already, we see that the only possible options are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/4/4e43d6823f7c60576b581c14ff0a2c3efc4fbe72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 1010$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"74\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/e/c9e206a6ce37a9faf3353963e4c3ca87fed0e392.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(D) } 1013$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"74\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>We need there to be no <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/a/a3a59bb1293ee3f6dec19de4019a7178874219ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />'s on the board at the end, so we attempt to convert them into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/a/39a710e66595fc1698f6d09b7f91ea01db604fcd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\normalsize o$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> while retaining as many existing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/a/39a710e66595fc1698f6d09b7f91ea01db604fcd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\normalsize o$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />'s as possible.\n</p><p>Notice that converting 4 <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/a/a3a59bb1293ee3f6dec19de4019a7178874219ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />'s into an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/a/39a710e66595fc1698f6d09b7f91ea01db604fcd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\normalsize o$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is not possible. We can apply an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/b/ecbb5d1ce9af02f00eb4c8d3fad8bca10c3fa73e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Additive \\, operation$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"152\" height=\"18\" /> on 3 <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/a/a3a59bb1293ee3f6dec19de4019a7178874219ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />'s and 1 <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/a/39a710e66595fc1698f6d09b7f91ea01db604fcd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\normalsize o$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> to get back 1 <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/a/39a710e66595fc1698f6d09b7f91ea01db604fcd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\normalsize o$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/c/a6cd60d3987f4c4be0fe49c85515c4a7474449d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e+e+e+\\normalsize o=\\normalsize o$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"136\" height=\"14\" />) By doing so, we retain all the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/a/39a710e66595fc1698f6d09b7f91ea01db604fcd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\normalsize o$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />'s we use in an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/c/04c62d78405c31d894a49670a6d648150038432f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$operation$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"17\" /> (and don't generate any new ones). In the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/7/e5711c8d31d3bc3119aba377c9bda0f9dfb14e4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2024$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" /> numbers, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/3/d83eeb9ab5890602a512b7735f593abec1dc6978.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1012$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/a/39a710e66595fc1698f6d09b7f91ea01db604fcd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\normalsize o$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />'s. This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/4/014eb288d68712ca669d4d034173ff148cc78219.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\le 1012$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"73\" height=\"16\" />, and the only option left is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/e/6ae0e6543fa9c66280df1b976860b4cb3d1dbd3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) } 1010}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"85\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p><br />\nNote: For the exact steps to arrive at 1010 odd numbers, perform\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/5/a650de49fa2d7bbc95a0f67a21b585ab0f855715.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e+e+e+o=o$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"136\" height=\"14\" /> (337 times)\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0dbc8ba7866d950d25d27e06568412337443ca3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e+o+o+o=o$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"136\" height=\"14\" /> (1 time)\n</p><p>~laythe_enjoyer211\n</p><p>~minor edit by MathCrafter314\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28guessing_strategy.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(guessing_strategy)\">Solution 3 (guessing strategy)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (guessing strategy)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that with every step, Jerry removes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> numbers and adds <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> number to the board. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> numbers are removed from the board in every step. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/2/5a2a6faa2842d28f63dfb8e8b7c823f1343b462c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2024\\equiv2\\pmod{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"144\" height=\"20\" />, the answer choice must also be congruent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/5/15504bd6556559dd3d8db32fccee4c68f8e7fe7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1010$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/4/764b059fd41cd1b6b1b0b4841681f7d9c0b2f789.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1013$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> among the answer choices satisfy this condition. This alone eliminates three choices, and one can guess from here for a 3 point expected value. \n</p><p>However, we start out with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/3/d83eeb9ab5890602a512b7735f593abec1dc6978.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1012$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> even numbers and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/3/d83eeb9ab5890602a512b7735f593abec1dc6978.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1012$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> odd numbers, and it is is not possible to get more odds than there were initially (every time we add or multiply four numbers, we can only produce one odd number, which cannot occur if only even numbers are used; therefore, there cannot be more odd numbers after an operation than before it). Thus, we choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/4/434caab571590d9400c63d2f316db94278e3e0df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) } 1010.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"90\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~Elephant200\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28OEEE.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(OEEE)\">Solution 4 (OEEE)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (OEEE)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/3/d83eeb9ab5890602a512b7735f593abec1dc6978.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1012$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> odd numbers and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/3/d83eeb9ab5890602a512b7735f593abec1dc6978.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1012$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> even numbers. In order to maximize the remaining numbers, then we must minimize the number of times the operation is performed.\n</p><p>Since we want to be left with all odd numbers, then we must get rid of the even numbers as quick as possible, which implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/1/511e48db3da8daf2efa43396b0a5f23b99272ad9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EEEE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />. This doesn't give an odd product or sum, so our next best option is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/a/d0a0925a51acbbb74feaa4de1b65a3eb1d1449e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OEEE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />, which gives an odd sum. \n</p><p>The maximum number of times this operation can be performed with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/a/d0a0925a51acbbb74feaa4de1b65a3eb1d1449e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OEEE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/8/f382607b128c1717ea577f5f6e7a2c7f5c08c5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\lfloor{\\dfrac{1012}{3}}\\right\\rfloor=337$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"114\" height=\"45\" />. This will eliminate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/3/af3b990b7af3c52062c92908131fa99c4aae9c4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\cdot337=1011$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"112\" height=\"14\" /> even numbers and no odd numbers (because each time the operation is performed, one odd number is eliminated but another one is created). \n</p><p>Therefore after the operation is performed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/d/c8d4bb13f188c6b23f37880c1c3cebfdcc415c6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$337$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" /> times with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/a/d0a0925a51acbbb74feaa4de1b65a3eb1d1449e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OEEE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />, there will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> even number left and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/3/d83eeb9ab5890602a512b7735f593abec1dc6978.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1012$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> odd numbers left. Performing this operation one more time with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/c/6dc64e6bef06f780e6e966eaf147c7b58a7c759b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EOOO$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"59\" height=\"14\" /> will give <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> even numbers and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/7/667cb5ddf6ae808aed2c00830b4a3053b9b98d90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(A) }1010}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"80\" height=\"30\" /> odd numbers. ~Tacos_are_yummy_1\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28EEEE.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(EEEE)\">Solution 5 (EEEE)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (EEEE)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/3/d83eeb9ab5890602a512b7735f593abec1dc6978.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1012$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> odd numbers and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/3/d83eeb9ab5890602a512b7735f593abec1dc6978.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1012$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> even numbers. Our goal is to get rid of all the even numbers. By performing the operation with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/1/511e48db3da8daf2efa43396b0a5f23b99272ad9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EEEE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />, we will remove <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> even numbers and create one simultaneously.\n</p><p>First, we can perform <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/1/511e48db3da8daf2efa43396b0a5f23b99272ad9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EEEE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> a maximum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/c/24c9e6fc5068fff38f6b9cec22798fb2e17c542a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1012}{4}=253$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"94\" height=\"38\" /> times, to end up with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/f/ecf0e2685a2e407dac4123db730639987e6083f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1012-4\\cdot253+253=253$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"211\" height=\"15\" /> even numbers. Performing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/1/511e48db3da8daf2efa43396b0a5f23b99272ad9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EEEE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> again <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/9/fe96fb20737de207ea83ca69b653f842543fd2d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\lfloor{\\dfrac{253}{4}}\\right\\rfloor=63$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"96\" height=\"45\" /> times will result in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a591a3951a5d67438e2db813ef3455da9877e29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$253-4\\cdot63+63=64$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"175\" height=\"15\" /> even numbers left. Repeating this process, eventually there will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> even number left and still <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/3/d83eeb9ab5890602a512b7735f593abec1dc6978.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1012$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> odd numbers. Performing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/c/81c87a2b54d9caa772c6f40eeaeb7a635f612230.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OOOE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"59\" height=\"14\" /> gives the answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/7/667cb5ddf6ae808aed2c00830b4a3053b9b98d90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(A) }1010}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"80\" height=\"30\" />. ~Tacos_are_yummy_1 ~ AVTV MINOR EDITS\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6_.28Monovariants.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(Monovariants)\">Solution 6 (Monovariants)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (Monovariants)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that the number of odd integers is monotonically decreasing, and further observe that the number of odd integers is preserved after an operation where Jerry adds three evens and one odd together, producing an odd number. To maximise the number of odd integers, we will use this operation whenever possible.\n</p><p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/3/d83eeb9ab5890602a512b7735f593abec1dc6978.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1012$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> even integers; to perform the specific procedure outlined above, we remove <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> even integers each time. Therefore, we will arrive in a situation where there is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> even integers and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/3/d83eeb9ab5890602a512b7735f593abec1dc6978.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1012$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> odd integers. To ensure that after the final operation, there will only be odd integers, we add the even integer and three odd integers, yielding one odd integer. There are now <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/5/15504bd6556559dd3d8db32fccee4c68f8e7fe7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1010$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> integers, all of them odd, so we select <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/f/73f27388b2df8e5b980da0178da8ddb38c9fe43f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{ (A) 1010 }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"88\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~LeonQS\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7\">Solution 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/3/d83eeb9ab5890602a512b7735f593abec1dc6978.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1012$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> odd integers, so the choices D and E are not possible. If the numbers 1 and 3 were erased, they would not be able to be recreated, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/3/d83eeb9ab5890602a512b7735f593abec1dc6978.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1012$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> - <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/f/73f27388b2df8e5b980da0178da8ddb38c9fe43f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{ (A) 1010 }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"88\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~turtleinexile\n~ note: if stuff is messed up here it's because i suck at latex. sorry\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_8\">Solution 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Like Solution 4, we'll use <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/a/d0a0925a51acbbb74feaa4de1b65a3eb1d1449e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OEEE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />, and they already explained why it maximizes the number of odd integers. Consider the set of integers between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. Optimally, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/7/2279dfd5bfac0badae18c78a178ed2f0f9eb4fb4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\equiv 0 \\pmod{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"115\" height=\"18\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/a/d0a0925a51acbbb74feaa4de1b65a3eb1d1449e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OEEE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> uses <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> even integers (&amp; the number of even integers is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/8/39876a50c8f30e868af0317946093f92fc674847.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left \\lfloor \\frac{n}{2} \\right\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"35\" height=\"35\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />). In that case, the max number of odd integers remaining is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/7/f275b1f33e3c37ece0e41964f0bcb806e95b46b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"13\" height=\"33\" /> where no odd integer is removed without being replaced.\n</p><p>The closest multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to the number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/7/e5711c8d31d3bc3119aba377c9bda0f9dfb14e4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2024$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/b/0cb39dbc06a6cd0a0f4e4dd1e3ff461fb7026ba6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2022$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />. A maximum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/e/6ce7e7e796ef6786e471adc9586c4c0bbc1703cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1011$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> odd integers can be left if the process is done for the integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/b/0cb39dbc06a6cd0a0f4e4dd1e3ff461fb7026ba6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2022$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />. Finally, there's <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> even number left, so the operation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/c/81c87a2b54d9caa772c6f40eeaeb7a635f612230.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OOOE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"59\" height=\"14\" /> is performed, thus the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/6/9564c4efd9a68406d5c9aae2d7e8b3e76584c131.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1011 + 1 - 2 = \\fbox{ (A) 1010 }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"212\" height=\"30\" /> since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/7/0873e9fed23538e535ac05c3284b86bd7bce6fd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2023$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> is another odd integer not between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/b/0cb39dbc06a6cd0a0f4e4dd1e3ff461fb7026ba6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2022$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, but the operation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/c/81c87a2b54d9caa772c6f40eeaeb7a635f612230.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OOOE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"59\" height=\"14\" /> removes a net <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> odd integers.\n</p><p>~iambaconiamgod\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_9\">Solution 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can remove <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> evens and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> odd every turn and do this <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/d/c8d4bb13f188c6b23f37880c1c3cebfdcc415c6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$337$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" /> times until we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> even number remaining and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/3/d83eeb9ab5890602a512b7735f593abec1dc6978.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1012$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> odd numbers because in every group of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> we lose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> evens, and one odd, but gain the odd back as the sum of the group will always be odd. With <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/4/764b059fd41cd1b6b1b0b4841681f7d9c0b2f789.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1013$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> integers left we remove a group of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> containing the one even and add back their odd some so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/b/1cb4d1c17cd7ce7e41fb5f6d333065189eccdba0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1013 - 4 + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"101\" height=\"15\" /> equals A, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/7/5b7718885d625c843cb2a1871fce32e4c1615a31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{1010}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"49\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~jamespudi\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_Pi_Academy_.28Fast_and_Easy_.E2.9A.A1.F0.9F.9A.80.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_Pi_Academy_(Fast_and_Easy_⚡🚀)\">Video Solution 1 by Pi Academy (Fast and Easy ⚡🚀)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by Pi Academy (Fast and Easy ⚡🚀)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/c6nhclB5V1w?feature=shared\">https://youtu.be/c6nhclB5V1w?feature=shared</a>\n</p><p>~ Pi Academy\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution 2 by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2 by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uKT6ormxQYE\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uKT6ormxQYE</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_3_by_Ani_lytical\">Video Solution 3 by Ani_lytical</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 3 by Ani_lytical\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofol